{"id": 51, "ts": 1784218156.282926, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the strongest overall fit.\u202fWhile we have now confirmed that Candidate\u202fC lacks evidence of crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication\u2014and, as the notes state, \u201csometimes is not good at taking criticism\u201d\u2014these gaps reinforce the concerns about his teamwork and feedback orientation.\u202fCandidate\u202fA does create a positive atmosphere with his crew and can decide quickly, but his documented difficulty communicating ideas and being regarded as egocentric still pose serious risks for cockpit coordination.\u202fCandidate\u202fD continues to show excellent reliability and problem\u2011solving, yet we still have no data on his crew\u2011cooperation, communication style, or ability to accept feedback, and his hot temper and arrogance remain unmitigated.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s proven reliability (\u201cvery conscientious\u201d), stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d), and technical competence (strong weather\u2011assessment) directly address the core safety\u2011critical criteria.\u202fAlthough his interpersonal flaws (nasty remarks, pretentious tone, weak memory for numbers) are not ideal, they are less likely to jeopardize safety than the unresolved teamwork deficiencies of the other candidates.\u202fTherefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fB for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
